T7 — Download / processing instructions (TWO paths)

The 47 runs are NOT one dataset. Only the 20 dRNA-seq runs go through TSSpredator (T10);
the other 27 (Capp-Switch, 5' RNA-seq) use the papers' published TSS tables. See docs/PIPELINE.md
for the full rationale. (This supersedes the old single-list instructions, which downloaded
all 47 locally with fastq-dump.)

============================================================
PATH A — 20 dRNA-seq runs (C. difficile) -> TSSpredator (T10)
============================================================
Run this on the machine that will run TSSpredator — don't pull tens of GB to a laptop and
re-upload. sra-tools (prefetch, fasterq-dump) is in the TSS env built from
infrastructure/conda-environments/environment-bio.yml (see docs/SETUP.md).

  conda activate promoter-mining-bio
  cd <work dir>            # a volume with tens of GB free

  # fetch only the 20 TSSpredator-compatible runs
  prefetch --option-file <repo>/data-acquisition-and-curation/tss-literature/SRR_dRNAseq_for_TSSpredator.txt
  for srr in $(cat <repo>/data-acquisition-and-curation/tss-literature/SRR_dRNAseq_for_TSSpredator.txt); do
      fasterq-dump --split-3 "$srr" -O . && gzip -f "${srr}"*.fastq
  done

  # then, in T10 — data-acquisition-and-curation/cdifficile-drnaseq/run_tss_pipeline.sh does all of
  # this (stage 2 downloads the reads itself, so the loop above is optional):
  #  - align to the CONFIRMED C. difficile assembly
  #    (630 = AM180355 / NC_009089; 630Delta-erm = its own assembly — see docs/PIPELINE.md)
  #  - build coverage/wiggle tracks
  #  - run TSSpredator with the correct TEX+/TEX- pairing (the committed .conf files)

============================================================
PATH B — 27 Capp-Switch + 5' RNA-seq runs -> published TSS tables
============================================================
Do NOT reprocess these with TSSpredator (they have no TEX- control). The papers' supplementary
TSS tables are used instead, and both are already in the repo:

  - Hocq 2022 (Microbiol Spectr, doi:10.1128/spectrum.02288-21)
    C. acetobutylicum ATCC 824, C. beijerinckii NCIMB 8052 / DSM 6423 (~12,114 mapped TSS).
    Committed as tss-literature/published_tss/hocq2022_cac_tss.xlsx; build_published_tss.sh
    (Phase A) turns it into the 5,759 in-genus training positives.
  - Al-Bassam 2018 (Nat Commun, doi:10.1038/s41467-018-06993-6)
    C. ljungdahlii ATCC 55383. This is VALIDATION truth, committed as
    evaluation-and-calibration/ljungdahlii_holdout_tss.tsv (1,245 primary TSS). Never put an
    Al-Bassam table in tss-literature/published_tss/: build_published_tss.sh would ingest it as
    training positives.

  (The raw runs stay in the per-method CSVs if a non-TSSpredator caller is ever needed.)

Tip: check installation with `fasterq-dump --version` (sra-tools).
